hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-16 : List (List Word)
hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-lines-16 = cons "*Synthesis*, *syn* + *tithenai*, putting together. *Synesthesia*, *syn* + *aisthēsis*, perceiving together. *Aesthetic*, *anesthesia* and *synesthesia* share the perceiving. Synthetic synesthesia is a putting-together of perceivings-together: perception assembled, which is what every reader of a script is, and what every developer navigating a scene is. *Hallucination* is from Latin *alucinari*, to wander in mind. Manufactured hallucination is guided wandering. A good interface is a guided wandering through information space, where the guide is the person's own intention." (cons "" nil)
